I am sitting at the table.
A young waiter comes to my table.
He has a tray in his hands.
My tea and bun maska are on the tray.
My table is a little small.
I make some space on the table.
"Will you please put the tea here?" I ask.
"Yes, Madam," the waiter says.
He puts the plate of bun maska on the table.
Then he puts the glass of tea.
"Will you give me a napkin?" I ask.
"Yes, Madam, I will give it right away," he says.
He gives me a napkin.
"Thank you, Dada," I say.
"Welcome, Madam," he says with a smile.
He goes to another table.
I put my phone aside.
The tea is very hot.
The tea smells very nice.
I happily drink my tea.
